  "liner": {
   "body_md": "This audience recording captures the Mountain Goats performing at the Rocket Bar in St. Louis, Missouri, on Saturday, October 10, 1998 [1]. The forty-one minute set contains thirteen songs, representing show twenty-two of four hundred and sixty-seven archived performances for the band [3]. The lineup includes early tracks like \"Going to Jamaica\" and \"Evening In Stalingrad,\" the latter being the earliest archived version with only two other archived performances [1][3]. Notably, the set features \"The Doll Song,\" \"New Math,\" and \"Adultery (The Extra Glenns),\" all of which are legendary because they are the only archived performances of these songs [1][3]. It also includes \"Infidelity (The Extra Glenns),\" a mythic rare track with just two archived performances [1][3]. The recording is the only one available for this date and has received a rating of three out of five stars from one listener [1]. A review of this specific recording by ThatGuyWhoReviewedEveryMountainGoatsRecording in 2016 notes that the set includes a couple of Extra Glenns songs for good measure [2]. The previous archived show for the band was on April 23, 1998, at the Blackwatch Pub [3].",
